@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "St Bluishbyrd";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<div class="columncontainer3-2">
    <img src="~/images/camp.png" width=90% height=90%/>
    <div>
        <div class="stickynote"><h4>Current food levels: 6</h4>
        <p>Parties can leave camp with <strong>6</strong> day's rations.</p></div>
        <div class="stickynote"><h4>Current security: Medium</h4></div>
        <p>The surrounding <strong>2</strong> hexes away from the town are safer and can be traversed quickly with no risk. </p>
        <div class="stickynote"><h4>Diplomacy: 80%</h4></div>
        <p>The queen empress and the kobold nation are more or less satisfied with your actions. </p>
    </div>

</div>
<div>
    <h2>Residents</h2>
    <br />
    <h3>Nana Coralyn</h3>
    <p>Nana is the local shopkeep, distinguishable by finding the largest,
         most extravagant building in the camp. She drives a hard bargain but 
         has been sponsoring tipoffs of nearby ruins.</p>
         <button> <a asp-area="" asp-controller="Town" asp-action="NanasEmporium">Enter Store</a></button>
    <h3>Karst</h3>
    <p>Karst is the human sheriff who spearheaded the expedition into the
        forsaken continent. He often lingers near the supply area, helping with logistics and mapping.
    </p>
    <h3>Sister Mary</h3>
    <p>Sister Mary is a spry woman who has recently set up shop near the camp. 
        With her trusty golem butler Jeremiah, she has rapidly erected a herbal 
        remedy store, selling potions and cures. 
    </p>
    <h3>Galena Arnsdottir</h3>
    <p>Galena is an orc tinsmith, who shyly peddles her trade to those in need
        of a sturdy pot or pan. 
    </p>
    <h3>Dervon</h3>
    <p>Dervon is a sturdily built dwarf who takes pride in his labourer business, powered by his skeletal "lads".
        Jovial but self-serving. </p>
    <h3>Frank</h3>
    <p>Frank is a short, tired looking goblin who defected from the forces of Gwimbly after he got sick of their methods. 
        He has become a reliable face around the camp to help with woodworking and general logistics. 
    </p>
    <h3>Tall Tree</h3>
    <p>An awakened tree has taken permanent residence in camp, providing a modicum of shade for any who seek it.
        The Great Tree occassionally looks through the tree, and may converse with those nearby. 
    </p>
    <h3>Flumphs</h3>
    <p>A cloister of flumphs seek peaceful communion amongst the camp, 
        and offer their psychic healing to those in need.
    </p>


</div>